WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:19.320
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.070
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:37.780
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.250
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:37.670
To live up to his brother Sieg's expectations, Leon activates Golden Castle of Stromberg.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:43.220
But it was a trap to destroy Kaiba Corporation's duel data.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.450
Unless Golden Castle is destroyed, the computer virus won't stop.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:53.660
But traps and spells don't work against it!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:59.660
KC Grand Prix Finale

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:09.150
You think you can destroy Golden Castle of Stromberg?

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.590
Yeah!

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:17.020
But even if Leon surrenders or loses the duel, the virus program won't stop!

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.820
And traps and spells don't work on that card!

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.290
How can Yugi destroy it?

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.560
Big brother?

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.990
Running away, Kaiba?

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.560
This duel is Yugi’s fight.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.930
I have my own fights to fight.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.860
Wait, big brother!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.210
You can't do anything anymore.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.880
Let’s continue the duel, Leon.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.880
Battle me with all your strength.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.370
And I’ll fight with all of mine.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.880
For every duelist, we can’t lose.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.880
And we'll save Leon too.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.250
Yeah.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.920
Yugi…

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.820
I can't take back what I did.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.970
But if there’s still hope for salvation, I'll trust Yugi!

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.920
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.620
Pointless.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.090
Golden Castle of Stromberg’s effect activates!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.720
Dark Magician Girl is moving on her own!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.310
Dark Magician Girl is gone!

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.240
Yugi also lost life points!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.170
No way...

00:03:53.510 --> 00:04:00.790
As long as Golden Castle of Stromberg is in play, you’re forced to battle each turn.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.780
When the opponent's monster attacks...

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:10.660
...the opponent takes damage equal to half its attack points, and the monster is destroyed.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.190
That effect isn't fair!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.600
It's crazy!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:19.670
That's why there was a risk for using that card.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.550
It's supposed to have a high maintenance cost.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.390
Get rid of all programs that the virus infiltrated!

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.620
Don't let the damage spread!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.090
Yes sir!

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.910
Big brother, I’ll help too!

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.000
Mokuba…

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.310
Okay.  You’re in charge of E-Level security.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.090
Leave it to me!

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.320
Leon did everything he could for Sieg.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.680
I can't forgive Sieg for betraying his brother.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.280
I won't let him have his way!

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.020
Spells and traps won't work.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.640
If I summon a monster, it's forced to attack, and I'll lose life points.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.910
But if I don't, I’ll be attacked directly.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.670
At this rate, I can't win.  However...

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.590
Yugi…

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.760
Don’t give up, Leon!

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.740
I’m not giving up!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.700
I’ll fight to the very end and break this trap!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.100
I set one card.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.270
I end my turn.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:37.730
Yugi - a true duelist that I admire - is battling me with all his strength.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.480
So I’ll believe in him and battle!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.230
My turn!

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:43.900
I draw!

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.740
I said that there's nothing you can do.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.180
This card is an invincible castle!

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.940
To maintain Golden Castle of Stromberg...

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:58.600
...you must send half your deck to the graveyard during the Standby Phase.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.040
And this cost is paid by the opponent!

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.610
What?

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:08.660
Why does the opponent have to pay the maintenance cost?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.080
Did he rewrite the original text data?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:20.530
This card is supposed to be hard to use because of its high maintenance cost.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:24.440
But he switched that burden to the opponent.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.470
Brother, how could you!

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:31.410
Yugi Muto, send half your deck to the graveyard.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.790
Damn!  Can’t something be done?

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:40.960
Damn!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:46.120
Leonheart, summon a Level 4 or lower monster from your deck.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.830
Brother…

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:53.830
Regardless of how this duel turns out, the virus can no longer be stopped.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:59.270
It’s only a matter of time until Kaiba Corporation’s main computer is a blank slate.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.740
Okay!

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.210
Beaver Warrior attacks!

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.130
Huh?  What's wrong?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.070
Mine is acting weird too.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:13.330
Go ahead and continue this charade until everything is gone.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.110
Continue, Leon.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.460
I summon Forest Wolf in attack position.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:27.300
Golden Castle of Stromberg forces it to battle!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.470
Oh no!  Yugi has no monsters on his field!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.640
Yugi!

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.810
This will end it!

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.050
Yugi!

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.880
I flip over my set card!

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.660
Dark Magic Retribution!

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:56.830
When you attack, I can Special Summon a Spellcaster from my graveyard!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.830
Come out, Dark Magician Girl!

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:11.880
The Spellcaster resurrected by Dark Magic Retribution is destroyed after the Battle Phase.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:14.580
He managed to survive.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.240
But if nothing changes...

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:21.920
His deck will shrink every turn, leaving him in a worse position.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.350
I end my turn.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.030
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:32.290
It's been three turns since Spinning Wheel Spindle activated.

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:34.970
So Queen's Knight resurrects!

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.900
I set two cards.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:43.080
I activate the spell card, Card of Sanctity from my hand!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:49.680
We both draw until we have six cards in our hands!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:57.350
I summon King's Knight in attack position!

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:02.520
When Queen's Knight and King's Knight are both on my field...

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.660
...I can Special Summon Jack's Knight from my deck!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:17.970
Even if you summon powerful monsters, they’re useless against Golden Castle of Stromberg.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.910
Are you sure?

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:25.250
I activate the spell card, Royal Straight!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:31.590
By tributing Queen's Knight, King's Knight and Jack's Knight...

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:37.700
...I can Special Summon Royal Straight Slasher from my deck, hand or graveyard.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.680
I activate Royal Straight Slasher’s effect!

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:01.520
By sending monsters Level 1 thru 5 from my deck to the graveyard...

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.510
...I destroy all cards on your field!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.990
Now there's an idea!

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.590
Monster effects can destroy that card!

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.820
Level 1, Kuriboh!

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.920
Level 2, Old Vindictive Magician!

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:23.300
Level 3, Giant Soldier of Stone!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.900
Level 4, Big Shield Gardna!

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.270
Level 5, Curse of Dragon!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.820
Go, Royal Straight Slasher!

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.620
Ultimate Five Crush!

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:53.630
Yeah!

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.430
He did it!

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.510
Why?

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.060
Why wasn’t it destroyed?

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.400
Something’s wrong!

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.340
Too bad.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.340
You did something!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:44.280
When he rewrote the text data, he negated monster effects too.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:47.280
You're such a cheater!

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:49.460
So there’s nothing he can do?

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:54.330
I activate the spell card, Time Travel from my hand!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:12:01.270
I remove my monster from play until your next Standby Phase.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.200
I end my turn.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:08.880
You removed your monster from play so that it's not forced to battle this turn.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.810
Pointless.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:15.520
Leonheart, time to bring down the curtains!

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.350
Yugi…

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:25.730
I still trust you!

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:28.170
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:34.460
Yugi Muto, pay Golden Castle's maintenance cost by sending half your deck to the graveyard.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.400
Sorry, I can't.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.840
What?

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:41.780
Look!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:49.720
I only have one card in my deck, so I can't pay half my deck.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:53.220
So Golden Castle of Stromberg is destroyed!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.160
What?  No way!

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.470
Yugi!

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:05.460
So that’s what Yugi was going for!

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:08.470
Yes.  Spell nor traps work on that card.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:13.220
And you're forced to battle, and it deflects monsters' attacks.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.190
But that card isn't invincible.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:20.160
Right.  Games have unexpected pitfalls.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.780
Well done, the other Yugi.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:33.520
Big brother, the virus program has stopped!

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:38.860
He found the card’s weakness.

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:41.270
I see!  Yugi did it!

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:44.340
Connect all programs to the backup system!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.540
Reboot the system!  Now!

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:54.160
How's that!  He foiled your plan!

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:00.710
I’m surprised you were able to destroy Golden Castle of Stromberg.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.030
But I’ll still win!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.210
Sore loser.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:12.430
My virus has already infiltrated deep into Kaiba Corporation’s main computer.

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.840
So it's affected all the duel systems.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:19.560
Destroying Golden Castle is too little, too late.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.950
And you only have one card in your deck!

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.580
Your next draw is your last one!

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:29.520
When you can't draw a card, you lose!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.840
Yugi…

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:36.500
I'm satisfied with getting this far.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.290
So I'll now...

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:43.420
Leon, no matter how bad the situation...

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.160
...I’ll keep dueling as long as I have a card in my deck!

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:52.500
Now that the despicable trap is gone, our real duel can now begin!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.270
Bring it!

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.000
Yugi…

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:56.440
Okay!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:04.180
Royal Straight Slasher - which was gone due to Time Travel - returns to the field!

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.620
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.340
Monster Reborn!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.790
It Special Summons Prinzessin from my graveyard!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:17.730
When Prinzessin is summoned, I can Special Summon Pumpkin Carriage!

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.330
I tribute Prinzessin and Pumpkin Carriage!

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.340
I summon Hexe Trude in attack position!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.640
Here I go, Yugi!

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.440
Hexe Trude attacks!

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:36.700
Destiny Crush!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:48.040
Hexe Trude gains 400 attack points each time it destroys your monster.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.450
I end my turn.

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:56.400
He has a monster with 3000 attack points, but Yugi only has one card in his deck!

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.320
Can he do anything with just one card?

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.080
He has to.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:04.490
Once he's out of cards to draw, Yugi loses.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:07.180
Yugi hasn’t given up yet!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:13.520
I believe in my deck to the end.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.720
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.990
I set one card.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.300
I activate the spell card, Emergency Provisions from my hand!

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:34.430
For every spell or trap card I send to the graveyard, I regain 1000 life points!

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:37.880
I activate the spell card, Monster Reborn!

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.290
Can it be?

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:42.280
Come out, Dark Magician!

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.880
Dark Magician!

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:53.920
But Dark Magician has 2500 attack points.

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.260
It’s no match for Hexe Trude.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:00.800
I flip over my set card, Necromancy!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:08.240
It randomly summons four monsters from your graveyard in defense position.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:18.080
Each time one of those monsters is destroyed, Hexe Trude loses 600 attack points.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.520
I flip over my set card, Diffusion Wave-Motion!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:32.820
By paying 1000 life points, my Level 7 or higher Spellcaster can attack all your monsters!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.260
What?

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:42.130
Go, Dark Magician!

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:44.140
Black Magic!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.510
Yeah!  He did it!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:01.430
Yugi!

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:04.430
That’s my grandson for you!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.360
It was a wonderful duel.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.290
Impossible...

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:11.660
Leon…

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.230
Yugi…  I…

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:20.700
This was a heartbreaking duel, but you never gave up.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.020
You’re a true duelist.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.310
Yugi…

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:34.320
The result of this duel doesn't matter!

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:35.780
Sieg...

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:36.630
Brother!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:44.160
It'll take a long time for Kaiba Corporation’s computers to recover from the virus's damage.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:45.530
In the meantime...

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:48.080
You think I’d give you that opportunity?

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:52.000
You overestimated yourself, so you revealed too much.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.440
What?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.450
After your initial move, I started preparing for every contingency.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:02.760
My main computer is already restored.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.930
You didn’t affect anything!

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:09.080
I-Impossible!  I...

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.920
Stop, brother.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:12.800
Leonheart?

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:17.980
You know yourself that none of this will change anything.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:25.800
You're saying that I can’t beat Kaiba?

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:28.740
Not just me.  You can’t beat anyone.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:34.760
Brother, I learned something from this incident.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:37.020
Once you give up, it’s all over.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:42.420
But if you don’t give up and keep trying, you'll get something eventually.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:48.980
I can’t do what you want me to do, but I do want to help you.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:52.840
From now on, share your suffering with me.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.370
Leonheart...

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:01.790
Isono.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:11.220
Kaiba Corporation's KC Grand Prix tournament has determined the best duelist!

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:14.290
The Duel King is Yugi Muto!

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.090
We can finally go home to Japan!

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.010
I wanna eat Japanese food!

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:44.190
Once I finish my work here, I’ll go to Japan too.

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:46.190
We’ll be waiting!

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:48.210
Because I want to see Shizuka.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.130
Then don’t come!

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:53.130
Don’t overexert yourself, Sugoroku.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:56.130
C'mon, I'm still young-

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.650
Told you so.

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:05.470
Yugi, I didn’t get to duel you this time, but let’s duel again someday.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:08.480
Sure!  I’m looking forward to it!

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.300
Take care, darling!

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:12.140
Rebecca!

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:15.460
I’ll come visit you in Japan.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.120
S-Sure.  We'll be waiting.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.580
Hey!  What are you doing?

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.350
We readied a plane for you, but you’re gonna miss it!

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.290
Is it time already?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:27.820
Oh no!  We gotta hurry!

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:29.490
W-Wait for me!

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:14.460
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:30.180
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:36.020
Without a goal in mind

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:44.590
We just step towards our dream

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:50.230
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:58.700
Your eye will find it

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:04.510
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:12.650
Will touch your soul

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:15.910
In a duel

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:30.080
The KC Grand Prix ended successfully.

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:33.200
And we finally made it home to Japan!

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:37.590
By the way, Kaiba Corporation's stock rose after the event.

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:39.980
And Kaiba Land is doing good business.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:43.470
But I feel a little sad.

00:23:43.470 --> 00:23:50.220
Because the journey to recover the other Yugi's lost memories is about to begin.

00:23:50.220 --> 00:23:52.500
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Ultimate Game

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:54.130
Duel, standby!
